# ClariFin_OS — Canonical .gitignore
#
# ONLY committed artifacts are C64 forensic evidence and provenance documents.
# Everything else is either generated, cached, or IDE-local state.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPENDENCIES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
node_modules/
.kilo/node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BUILD OUTPUTS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
clarinfin_verification.egg-info/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CACHE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.turbo/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
memory-bank/
test-results/
dependency-reports/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ENVIRONMENT & SECRETS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.env
.env*.local
.env.production

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LOGS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*.log
npm-debug.log
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OS FILES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# IDE (keep root-level configs, ignore IDE-specific)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.vscode/
.idea/
.sublime-*
.cursor/
.kilo/plans/
.kilo/worktrees/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PYTHON VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENTS
# CANONICAL: Only repository-root .venv is allowed.
# backend/venv and backend/.venv are FORBIDDEN (M9-C42.5).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.venv/
backend/venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
env/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PYTHON CACHE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATABASE & DATA
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/
uploads/
# Exception: backend/src/data/ is source, never local data
!backend/src/data/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MISCELLANEOUS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.vercel
.expo/
.temp/
temp/
tmp/
unrelated/
servers/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MUTATION TESTING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
backend/mutants/
backend/run_mutmut_patched.sh
.mutmut-cache/
mutants/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# VERIFICATION PIPELINE GENERATED
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RUNTIME GENERATED — POLICY
#
# Policy: generated runtime output is ignored by default. Only the
# explicitly identified canonical evidence and contract/reference
# artifacts below remain version-controlled.
#
# Before this rule the ignore list enumerated individual files and
# directories, and three `!runtime/generated/m9-c64*` negations were
# scattered through it. That inverted the policy: ~4,400 regenerable
# files were tracked while the handful of genuinely canonical
# artifacts survived only because someone remembered to write an
# exception. Ignoring the subtree and re-including the canonical set
# makes an unlisted artifact ignored, which is the safe default.
#
# Anything added to the "canonical" list below must be justified as
# committed provenance/evidence or as a contract baseline that CI
# reads as an input. Regenerable output does not belong there.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The subtree is excluded by its immediate children rather than the directory
# itself: git never descends into an excluded directory, so `runtime/generated/`
# would make every `!` exception below unreachable for any *new* file. Matching
# `/*` keeps the canonical set genuinely re-includable.
/runtime/generated/*

# ── Canonical committed evidence (C64 forensic convergence) ──
# Forensic reconstruction evidence and provenance for the C64
# runtime-framework convergence milestones.
!/runtime/generated/m9-c64-r-runtime-pipeline-forensic-validation/
!/runtime/generated/m9-c64-r2-runtime-pipeline-attribution-reconciliation/
!/runtime/generated/m9-c64-runtime-framework-final-convergence/
!/runtime/generated/m9-c64-final-runtime-command-ci-convergence/

# ── Canonical committed evidence (M9-C71 mutation trust) ──
# The mutation-measurement trust certification bundle. Self-describing
# final certification and its supporting evidence. Written by
# runtime/foundation/verification/mutation_trust.py, which reads it
# back only to print it, so it is provenance rather than an input.
!/runtime/generated/m9-c71-mutation-trust/

# ── Canonical committed evidence (M9-C66 certification forensics) ──
!/runtime/generated/m9-c66-certification-forensics/

# ── Contract / reference artifacts ──
# frontend/generated/openapi-current.json is the committed API contract
# baseline that the API Contract Integrity gate diffs against
# (runtime/foundation/verification/api_contracts/gate.py), and
# toolchain-lock.json pins the frontend toolchain contract. These are
# inputs, not output, and are therefore version-controlled.
!frontend/generated/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GENERATED STATE THAT ESCAPED ITS ROOT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Several tools write through cwd-relative paths, so a run started from
# a subdirectory materialises a nested copy of the tree (a run from
# backend/ produced backend/runtime/generated/). These are runtime
# state by definition and must never be committed.
runtime/runtime/generated/
backend/runtime/generated/
frontend/runtime/generated/
.github/backend/

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS (keep only specific ones)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Backend test generated artifacts — regenerated deterministically by
# .github/scripts/run_fast_checks.sh (tools/development/check_coverage.py)
# from tracked inputs on every run, including a clean checkout.
backend/tests/generated/

# M9-C71 — mutation-measurement trust.
# The sentinel sink is per-run append-only execution evidence regenerated by
# every mutation shard; committing it would add a file that changes on every
# campaign and proves nothing about the code.
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/*-sentinel-sink.jsonl
# mutmut-generated mutants and bytecode caches are build artifacts.
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/mutants/
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/.mutmut-cache/
backend/tests/mutation_trust/canary/__pycache__/
